{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>When you vow a vow to HaShem your Elohim.</b> It is proper that your word be trusted by all. However, what you vow to HaShem your Elohim — not only are you obligated to fulfill it, but the fulfillment must also be without delay." "<b>For He will surely require it of you.</b> That if you delay fulfillment, He will exact it from you against your will." "<b>And there will be sin in you.</b> And even when you do fulfill it, if done in such a manner the punishment for the delay will still be upon you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:03.602381126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}